24
00:02:58.575 --> 00:03:13.389
<v Ananya Desai>Row-level security in Postgres. Every row carries the source ACL, and the query runs as the user. So you only ever see what you could already see in Slack or Gmail. That's non-negotiable, honestly. One leak and we're done.</v>

